<p>
  Donations and membership fees to <%= trust.name %> are voluntary
  contributions to charitable work. This policy explains when a refund is possible.
</p>

<h2>1. General rule</h2>
<p>
  Once a donation or membership fee is received, it is used for the Trust's
  charitable work and is generally <strong>not refundable</strong>.
</p>

<h2>2. When we will refund</h2>
<p>We will refund the amount in full if:</p>
<ul>
  <li>you were charged twice for the same payment (duplicate transaction);</li>
  <li>a wrong amount was charged because of a technical error;</li>
  <li>money was deducted but the payment failed and no receipt was issued;</li>
  <li>the payment was made without your permission (for example, a fraudulent card use).</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. How to ask for a refund</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Contact us within <strong>15 days</strong> of the payment.</li>
  <li>Give your name, transaction ID, amount, date and the reason for the refund.</li>
  <li>We may ask for proof such as a bank statement.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Processing</h2>
<ul>
  <li>We reply within 7 working days.</li>
  <li>Approved refunds are sent back to the original payment method through PayU within 7–10 working days.</li>
  <li>Any receipt or certificate issued for a refunded amount becomes invalid.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Cancellation</h2>
<p>
  A payment can be cancelled before it is completed on the payment page. Once
  it is completed, the refund rules above apply. Memberships cannot be
  cancelled for a partial refund.
</p>

